&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we&#39;re looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you&#39;re ready to help the world&#39;s best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you driven by the challenge of turning complex operational processes into seamless, high-performing systems? New Relic is looking for a Senior Revenue Operations Manager to own the technical and automation engine behind our Go-To-Market (GTM) organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the GTM Planning &amp;amp; Process team, you will sit right at the intersection of business strategy, field execution, and cutting-edge technology. You will serve as a strategic partner across our revenue organization, eliminating operational friction, scaling systems, and building solutions that directly impact our growth trajectory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM Strategy &amp;amp; Automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive the GTM technology roadmap (including Salesforce, Clay, and Salesloft). You will pilot emerging AI capabilities and transform manual steps into efficient, automated workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Execution &amp;amp; Quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with cross-functional stakeholders to gather requirements and translate business needs into clear user stories, technical specs, and UAT testing plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Governance &amp;amp; Analytics:&lt;/strong&gt; Define key system-level performance metrics, build automated dashboards, and collaborate with Data &amp;amp; Analytics to maintain a trusted source of truth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enablement &amp;amp; Change Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Guide field adoption of new system features by creating clear documentation, leading enablement sessions, and executing change management strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Marketing, Sales Operations, and Customer Adoption to streamline business rules and build a customer lifecycle (from initial land, onboarding, and adoption, to value realization and expansion)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role Requires:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in B2B SaaS across Revenue Operations, Field Sales Ops, or GTM Systems Architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong functional understanding of Salesforce (including how data flows and integrates between systems) alongside Business Intelligence tools like Tableau or advanced Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading cross-functional projects, writing detailed user stories, and managing delivery using Agile/Scrum methodologies in Jira.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong builder mindset with a knack for translating qualitative business needs into scalable technical designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant professional experience or a Bachelor’s degree in Business, Information Systems, Computer Science, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern GTM tools such as Salesforce CPQ, LeanData, or Clay.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to implementing AI capabilities for predictive scoring or automated routing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical SQL skills and familiarity with Snowflake or AWS data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An advanced degree (such as an MBA or related Master&#39;s degree).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-&lt;em&gt;KM&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The pay range below represents a reasonable estimate of the salary for the listed position. This role is eligible for a corporate bonus plan. Pay within this range varies by work location and may also depend on job-related factors such as an applicant’s skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New Relic provides a variety of benefits for this role, including healthcare, dental, vision, parental leave and planning, and mental health benefits, a 401(k) plan and match, flex time-off, 11 paid holidays, volunteer time-off, and other competitive benefits designed to improve the lives of our employees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Estimated Base Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$131,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$164,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fostering a diverse, welcoming and inclusive environment is important to us. We work hard to make everyone feel comfortable bringing their best, most authentic selves to work every day. We celebrate our talented Relics’ different backgrounds and abilities, and recognize the different paths they took to reach us – including nontraditional ones. Their experiences and perspectives inspire us to make our products and company the best they can be. We’re looking for people who feel connected to our mission and values, not just candidates who check off all the boxes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete any part of the application or recruiting process, please reach out to &lt;a ----- -----
&lt;p&gt;We believe in empowering all Relics to achieve professional and business success through a flexible workforce model. This model allows us to work in a variety of workplaces that best support our success, including fully office-based, fully remote, or hybrid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In compliance with applicable law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work and to complete employment eligibility verification. Note: Our stewardship of the data of thousands of customers means that a criminal background check is required to join New Relic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We will consider qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records based on individual circumstances and in accordance with applicable law including, but not limited to, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sfgov.org/olse/sites/default/files/FCO%20poster2020.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headhunters and recruitment agencies may not submit resumes/CVs through this website or directly to managers. New Relic does not accept unsolicited headhunter and agency resumes, and will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with New Relic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New Relic develops and distributes encryption software and technology that complies with U.S. export controls and licensing requirements. Certain New Relic roles require candidates to pass an export compliance assessment as a condition of employment in any global location. If relevant, we will provide more information later in the application process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are evaluated based on qualifications, regardless of race, religion, ethnicity, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression or identity, age, disability, neurodiversity, veteran or marital status, political viewpoint, or other legally protected characteristics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Review our Applicant Privacy Notice at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://newrelic.com/termsandconditions/applicant-privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://newrelic.com/termsandconditions/applicant-privacy-policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we&#39;re looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you&#39;re ready to help the world&#39;s best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Legal Counsel, EMEA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Legal Counsel (EMEA) based in the UK with deep SaaS commercial transaction experience to join our collaborative, forward-thinking legal team. At New Relic, legal isn’t just a support function, you will sit directly at the deal table, driving revenue growth, optimising customer and partner relationships, and scaling our SaaS business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will enjoy direct visibility, genuine autonomy, and the platform to curate your own career trajectory within a globally dispersed team. If you thrive in a dynamic environment, enjoy solving complex commercial challenges, and want to directly power our go-to-market strategy, this is the role for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structure &amp;amp; Close SaaS Deals:&lt;/strong&gt; Draft, review, and negotiate complex SaaS agreements, including data processing addenda and security terms in direct support of EMEA go-to-market efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower Sales Teams:&lt;/strong&gt; Coach and advise regional sales teams on SaaS deal structure, negotiation tactics, and customer dispute resolution to accelerate sales velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale Channel Partnerships:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Partner business teams to structure, negotiate, and expand business via resellers, MSPs, distributors, and global system integrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Privacy &amp;amp; Regulatory Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with Privacy Legal to embed practical risk-tolerance strategies and standardise commercial contract responses under global privacy regimes (GDPR, DORA, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Scalable Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Own, refine, and modernise SaaS agreement templates, negotiation playbooks, and contract escalation workflows to ensure legal scales alongside business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as a Trusted Advisor:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide pragmatic, risk-aware legal guidance across cross-functional partners, including Marketing, Product, Finance, and Contract Managers, aligning legal strategy with our consumption-based model, monetisation, and product-led growth (PLG) goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role requires&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mandatory SaaS Commercial Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Substantial experience drafting and negotiating complex SaaS commercial contracts, partner frameworks, and cloud technology agreements with a solid knowledge of revenue recognition principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educational &amp;amp; Qualification Background (UK): &lt;/strong&gt;Qualified to practice law and in good standing with the relevant professional regulatory body (e.g., state bar, Solicitors Regulation Authority, or equivalent) in your jurisdiction of residence&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy &amp;amp; Security Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid hands-on knowledge of data privacy, artificial intelligence, security topics, and global compliance frameworks within commercial SaaS transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM &amp;amp; Sales Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactive, strategic approach to working directly alongside enterprise sales teams to drive deal execution across the EMEA region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy &amp;amp; Resilience:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to manage competing deliverables, set clear boundaries, prioritise under deadlines, and operate independently in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Outstanding interpersonal skills with a track record of building trust across functions, regions, and executive levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house legal experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with consumption-based in SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience handling GSI/Reseller partner agreements and advising marketing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An eagerness to leverage AI, with a deep understanding of AI products, LLMs and the product lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Privacy certifications (e.g., CIPP/E) or deep familiarity with the EU AI Act and DORA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote #LI-JJ2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fostering a diverse, welcoming and inclusive environment is important to us. We work hard to make everyone feel comfortable bringing their best, most authentic selves to work every day. We celebrate our talented Relics’ different backgrounds and abilities, and recognize the different paths they took to reach us – including nontraditional ones. Their experiences and perspectives inspire us to make our products and company the best they can be. We’re looking for people who feel connected to our mission and values, not just candidates who check off all the boxes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete any part of the application or recruiting process, please reach out to &lt;a ----- -----
&lt;p&gt;We believe in empowering all Relics to achieve professional and business success through a flexible workforce model. This model allows us to work in a variety of workplaces that best support our success, including fully office-based, fully remote, or hybrid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In compliance with applicable law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work and to complete employment eligibility verification. Note: Our stewardship of the data of thousands of customers means that a criminal background check is required to join New Relic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We will consider qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records based on individual circumstances and in accordance with applicable law including, but not limited to, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sfgov.org/olse/sites/default/files/FCO%20poster2020.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headhunters and recruitment agencies may not submit resumes/CVs through this website or directly to managers. New Relic does not accept unsolicited headhunter and agency resumes, and will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with New Relic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New Relic develops and distributes encryption software and technology that complies with U.S. export controls and licensing requirements. Certain New Relic roles require candidates to pass an export compliance assessment as a condition of employment in any global location. If relevant, we will provide more information later in the application process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are evaluated based on qualifications, regardless of race, religion, ethnicity, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression or identity, age, disability, neurodiversity, veteran or marital status, political viewpoint, or other legally protected characteristics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Review our Applicant Privacy Notice at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://newrelic.com/termsandconditions/applicant-privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://newrelic.com/termsandconditions/applicant-privacy-policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Banyan Software is the best permanent home for software businesses that serve specialized industries, their employees, and their customers. With a buy-grow-and-hold-for-life approach and a permanent capital base, Banyan acquires and grows companies worldwide, honoring founder legacies and helping portfolio companies modernize through shared AI expertise and operational discipline. Founded in 2016, Banyan operates more than 120 portfolio companies across North and South America, Europe, and APAC, and has appeared on the Inc. 5000 list for six consecutive years. The Banyan Software Foundation, endowed with $100 million in Banyan stock, leverages technology to build a greener and more equitable world.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atamis is a growing software business based in Cardiff, providing analysis and management tools to organisations operating in complex commercial environments. As the company continues to scale, the team is expanding to meet increasing demand while maintaining a strong focus on delivering high-quality, long-term solutions to customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Atamis is seeking a&amp;nbsp;Product Manager who will be responsible for product planning. This includes managing the product throughout the Product Lifecycle, gathering and prioritising product and customer requirements, defining the product vision, and working closely with development and configuration, to deliver winning products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain a deep understanding of customer experience, identify, and fill product gaps and generate new ideas that grow market share, improve customer experience and drive growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create buy-in for the product vision both internally and with key external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the product roadmap and scheduling of planned work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Finance and Commercial to develop product pricing and positioning strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate product strategy into detailed requirements and prototypes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and prioritise activities based on business and customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Development and Configuration teams to deliver with quick time-to-market and optimal resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Marketing to drive product launches and maximising marketing opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate promotional plans to ensure that they are consistent with product line strategy and that the message is effectively conveyed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a product evangelist to build awareness and understanding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the company by visiting customers to solicit feedback on company products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse the feedback loops to identify product enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Director of Product Strategy as required to deliver the product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven work experience in product management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing all aspects of a successful product throughout its lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop product and marketing strategies and effectively communicate recommendations to executive management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid technical background with understanding and/or hands-on experience in software development and web technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and willingness to roll up one’s sleeves to get the job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at working effectively with cross functional teams in a matrix organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation Range - 60K - 65K GBP + Benefits &amp;amp; Bonus. Salary is based on a number of factors including market conditions, location and may vary depending on job-related skills and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Diversity, Equity, Inclusion &amp;amp; Equal Employment Opportunity at Banyan: Banyan affirms that inequality is detrimental to our Global Teams, associates, our Operating Companies, and the communities we serve. As a collective, our goal is to impact lasting change through our actions. Together, we unite for equality and equity. Banyan is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of any protected characteristic, including race, color, genetic information, creed, national origin, religion, sex, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, lawful alien status, ancestry, age, marital status, or protected veteran status and will not discriminate against anyone on the basis of a disability. We support an inclusive workplace where associates excel based on personal merit, qualifications, experience, ability, and job performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please Note&lt;/strong&gt;: Banyan Software does not accept unsolicited resumes or applications submitted via email, LinkedIn, or other direct channels. All candidates must apply through our official Careers site to be considered for employment. Applications submitted outside of our applicant tracking system will not be reviewed.&lt;/p&gt;
